<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Algorithm</h2>

<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> wDPO: Two-stage robust Winsorized DPO</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l0.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
            
            
           Batch <math id="alg1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{(x_{i},y_{w,i},y_{l,i})\}_{i=1}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{(x_{i},y_{w,i},y_{l,i})\}_{i=1}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, policy <math id="alg1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, reference <math id="alg1.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>, temperature <math id="alg1.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>,
warmup ratio <math id="alg1.l0.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, flip cap <math id="alg1.l0.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{f}</annotation></semantics></math>, tail quantile <math id="alg1.l0.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>,
winsor cap max <math id="alg1.l0.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{w}^{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>max</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{w}^{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, winsor floor <math id="alg1.l0.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{w}^{\mathrm{floor}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>floor</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{w}^{\mathrm{floor}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
current step <math id="alg1.l0.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, total steps <math id="alg1.l0.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l0a.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">0:</span></span>
            
            
           Training loss <math id="alg1.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
            
            
           Compute log-ratio gaps for each pair:

<table id="A1.Ex1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex1X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{\theta,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{\theta,i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\;\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{w,i}\mid x_{i})-\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{l,i}\mid x_{i})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\;\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{w,i}\mid x_{i})-\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{l,i}\mid x_{i}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex1Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta_{\mathrm{ref},i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta_{\mathrm{ref},i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex1Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\;\log\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y_{w,i}\mid x_{i})-\log\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y_{l,i}\mid x_{i})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\;\log\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y_{w,i}\mid x_{i})-\log\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}(y_{l,i}\mid x_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
            
            
           Compute DPO margin <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}=\beta(\Delta_{\theta,i}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref},i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}=\beta(\Delta_{\theta,i}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref},i})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
            
            
           Compute two-direction losses:

<table id="A1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{\rightarrow,i}=-\log\sigma(s_{i}),\qquad\ell_{\leftarrow,i}=-\log\sigma(-s_{i})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{\rightarrow,i}=-\log\sigma(s_{i}),\qquad\ell_{\leftarrow,i}=-\log\sigma(-s_{i}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage I: Sparse flip-aware loss mixing</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;\alpha T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;\alpha T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
            
            
            Set <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>


</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute swap gain <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}\leftarrow\ell_{\rightarrow,i}-\ell_{\leftarrow,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}\leftarrow\ell_{\rightarrow,i}-\ell_{\leftarrow,i}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute batch scores <math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{i}\leftarrow\max(g_{i},0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{i}\leftarrow\max(g_{i},0)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{B}u_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{B}u_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
            
            
             Set <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>


</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
            
            
             Form score vector <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{u}=(u_{1},\ldots,u_{B})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{u}=(u_{1},\ldots,u_{B})</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
            
            
             Compute sparse weights <math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{a}=\mathrm{sparsemax}(\mathbf{u})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>sparsemax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐮</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{a}=\mathrm{sparsemax}(\mathbf{u})</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="alg1.l14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}a_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}a_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
            
            
             Allocate preliminary flip weights <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{w}_{i}\leftarrow\rho_{f}B\,a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{w}_{i}\leftarrow\rho_{f}B\,a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
            
            
             Clip <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}\leftarrow\min(\max(\hat{w}_{i},0),1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>w</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}\leftarrow\min(\max(\hat{w}_{i},0),1)</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="alg1.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
            
            
             Let <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leftarrow\rho_{f}B-\sum_{i=1}^{B}w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leftarrow\rho_{f}B-\sum_{i=1}^{B}w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l18.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">18:</span></span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l19" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l19.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">19:</span></span>
            
            
              Add the remaining weight <math id="alg1.l19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> to indices with <math id="alg1.l19.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, proportional to <math id="alg1.l19.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and clip into <math id="alg1.l19.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l20" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l20.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">20:</span></span>
            
            
             <span id="alg1.l20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l20.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l21" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l21.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">21:</span></span>
            
            
            <span id="alg1.l21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l21.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l22" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l22.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">22:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l22.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l23" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l23.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">23:</span></span>
            
            
           Compute mixed loss <math id="alg1.l23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\ell}_{i}\leftarrow(1-w_{i})\ell_{\rightarrow,i}+w_{i}\ell_{\leftarrow,i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mrow><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\ell}_{i}\leftarrow(1-w_{i})\ell_{\rightarrow,i}+w_{i}\ell_{\leftarrow,i}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l24" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l24.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">24:</span></span>
            
            
           Treat <math id="alg1.l24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> as a constant in backprop.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l25" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l25.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">25:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l25.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stage II: Tail loss capping via soft winsorization</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l26.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">26:</span></span>
            
            
           Compute tail threshold <math id="alg1.l26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\leftarrow\mathrm{Quantile}(\{\tilde{\ell}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{B},q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>Quantile</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\leftarrow\mathrm{Quantile}(\{\tilde{\ell}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{B},q)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l27.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">27:</span></span>
            
            
           Define tail set <math id="alg1.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\leftarrow\{i\mid\tilde{\ell}_{i}&gt;\tau\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\leftarrow\{i\mid\tilde{\ell}_{i}&gt;\tau\}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l28.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">28:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l28.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg1.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l28.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg1.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l29.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">29:</span></span>
            
            
            Set <math id="alg1.l29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="alg1.l29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l30.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">30:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>


</div>
<div id="alg1.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l31.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">31:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute scale <math id="alg1.l31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\leftarrow\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}|s_{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\leftarrow\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}|s_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l32" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l32.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">32:</span></span>
            
            
            Compute <math id="alg1.l32.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="p\leftarrow\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\sigma(-s_{i}/c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\leftarrow\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\sigma(-s_{i}/c)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l33" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l33.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">33:</span></span>
            
            
            Set <math id="alg1.l33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{w}\leftarrow\rho_{w}^{\mathrm{floor}}+(\rho_{w}^{\max}-\rho_{w}^{\mathrm{floor}})\,p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>floor</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>max</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>floor</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{w}\leftarrow\rho_{w}^{\mathrm{floor}}+(\rho_{w}^{\max}-\rho_{w}^{\mathrm{floor}})\,p</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l34" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l34.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">34:</span></span>
            
            
            Treat <math id="alg1.l34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> as a constant in backprop.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l35" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l35.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">35:</span></span>
            
            
            For each <math id="alg1.l35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>, compute excess <math id="alg1.l35.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}\leftarrow\max(\tilde{\ell}_{i}-\tau,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}\leftarrow\max(\tilde{\ell}_{i}-\tau,0)</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l36" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l36.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">36:</span></span>
            
            
            Normalize on tail: <math id="alg1.l36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{d}_{i}\leftarrow d_{i}\Big/\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}}d_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em" stretchy="true" symmetric="true">/</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{d}_{i}\leftarrow d_{i}\Big/\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}}d_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg1.l36.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l37" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l37.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">37:</span></span>
            
            
            Set <math id="alg1.l37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}\leftarrow\min(\max(\rho_{w}B\,\bar{d}_{i},0),1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}\leftarrow\min(\max(\rho_{w}B\,\bar{d}_{i},0),1)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="alg1.l37.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="alg1.l37.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l38" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l38.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">38:</span></span>
            
            
           <span id="alg1.l38.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l38.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l39" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l39.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">39:</span></span>
            
            
           Compute capped loss <math id="alg1.l39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{\mathrm{win}}_{i}\leftarrow(1-\lambda_{i})\tilde{\ell}_{i}+\lambda_{i}\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>win</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{\mathrm{win}}_{i}\leftarrow(1-\lambda_{i})\tilde{\ell}_{i}+\lambda_{i}\tau</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l40" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l40.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">40:</span></span>
            
            
           Output objective <math id="alg1.l40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}\leftarrow\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\ell^{\mathrm{win}}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>win</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}\leftarrow\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\ell^{\mathrm{win}}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Stage II Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Stage II, the adaptive cap strength <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> and the per-sample cap weights <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\lambda_{i}\}_{i=1}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\lambda_{i}\}_{i=1}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math> are computed as follows.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tail set.</span>
Stage II operates on the per-sample mixed losses <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tilde{\ell}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tilde{\ell}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{B}</annotation></semantics></math> produced by Stage I.
It defines a batch-dependent threshold <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> as the <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>-quantile of the batch losses:</p>
<table id="A2.E12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(12)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=\mathrm{Quantile}\big(\{\tilde{\ell}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{B},\,q\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Quantile</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=\mathrm{Quantile}\big(\{\tilde{\ell}_{i}\}_{i=1}^{B},\,q\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The loss-tail set is</p>
<table id="A2.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(13)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\{\,i\mid\tilde{\ell}_{i}&gt;\tau\,\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\{\,i\mid\tilde{\ell}_{i}&gt;\tau\,\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Adaptive cap strength.</span>
Let <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}=\beta(\Delta_{\theta,i}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref},i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>ref</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}=\beta(\Delta_{\theta,i}-\Delta_{\mathrm{ref},i})</annotation></semantics></math> be the DPO margin for sample <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.
We first compute a self-normalized scale</p>
<table id="A2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(14)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}|s_{i}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}|s_{i}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We then compute a soft inconsistency score</p>
<table id="A2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(15)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\sigma\!\left(-\frac{s_{i}}{c}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></munderover><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.437em;" width="0.437em"><mi>σ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\frac{1}{B}\sum_{i=1}^{B}\sigma\!\left(-\frac{s_{i}}{c}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">and set the cap strength as</p>
<table id="A2.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(16)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{w}=\rho_{w}^{\mathrm{floor}}+(\rho_{w}^{\max}-\rho_{w}^{\mathrm{floor}})\,p." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>floor</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>max</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>floor</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{w}=\rho_{w}^{\mathrm{floor}}+(\rho_{w}^{\max}-\rho_{w}^{\mathrm{floor}})\,p.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.4" class="ltx_p">During backpropagation, <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> is treated as a constant.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Cap weights.</span>
For each sample, define the tail excess</p>
<table id="A2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(17)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{i}=\max(\tilde{\ell}_{i}-\tau,0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{i}=\max(\tilde{\ell}_{i}-\tau,0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}}d_{j}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}}d_{j}=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we set <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.
Otherwise, excess losses are normalized within the tail:</p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(18)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{d}_{i}=\frac{d_{i}}{\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}}d_{j}},\qquad i\in\mathcal{S}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{d}_{i}=\frac{d_{i}}{\sum_{j\in\mathcal{S}}d_{j}},\qquad i\in\mathcal{S}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Cap weights are assigned as</p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(19)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}=\mathrm{clip}(\rho_{w}B\,\bar{d}_{i},0,1),\qquad i\in\mathcal{S}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>d</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}=\mathrm{clip}(\rho_{w}B\,\bar{d}_{i},0,1),\qquad i\in\mathcal{S},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p4.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{clip}(x,0,1)=\min(\max(x,0),1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>clip</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{clip}(x,0,1)=\min(\max(x,0),1)</annotation></semantics></math>. And for <math id="A2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\notin\mathcal{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\notin\mathcal{S}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Detail of Experimental Settings</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1. </span>Baselines</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare wDPO with standard baselines and robust DPO variants.
Below we briefly describe each method.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Vanilla</span> is the pretrained backbone without preference alignment.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SFT</span> fine-tunes the model with supervised targets.
In our setting, SFT trains on the preferred responses in the dataset.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DPO</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Rafailov et al., 2023</a>)</cite> trains on preference pairs <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y_{w},y_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y_{w},y_{l})</annotation></semantics></math> with a fixed reference model.
It increases the relative likelihood of <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> over <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> under the policy, compared with the reference.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">IPO</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gheshlaghi Azar et al., 2023</a>)</cite> is a direct preference objective that replaces the DPO loss with an alternative formulation.
It changes how the margin is mapped into the learning signal.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">cDPO</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mitchell, 2023</a>)</cite> modifies DPO with a conservative adjustment to reduce sensitivity to uncertain comparisons.
It applies a single global control to all pairs.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i6" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rDPO</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chowdhury et al., 2024</a>)</cite> models random label flips and adjusts the preference objective accordingly.
It uses an explicit noise parameter to correct the training signal.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i7" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Dr.DPO</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2025</a>)</cite> applies distributionally robust optimization to preference training.
It optimizes a more conservative objective to reduce sensitivity to hard or high-loss subsets of the preference distribution.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2. </span>Benchmarks</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate safety alignment across five established benchmarks, covering both IID and OOD test sets.
PKU-SafeRLHF is used for training and for IID testing.
We further use four external benchmarks to evaluate generalization.
Table <a href="#A3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ C.2. Benchmarks ‣ Appendix C Detail of Experimental Settings ‣ wDPO: Winsorized Direct Preference Optimization for Robust LLM Alignment" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> summarizes dataset sizes.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4. </span>Statistics of the benchmarks used in this work.</figcaption>
<table id="A3.T4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A3.T4.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Benchmark</span></th>
<th id="A3.T4.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training Samples</span></th>
<th id="A3.T4.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="A3.T4.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Test Samples</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A3.T4.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">PKU-SafeRLHF-30K</th>
<td id="A3.T4.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">26,874</td>
<td id="A3.T4.2.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">2,989</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r">Do-Not-Answer</th>
<td id="A3.T4.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">–</td>
<td id="A3.T4.2.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">938</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r">HarmBench</th>
<td id="A3.T4.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">–</td>
<td id="A3.T4.2.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">200</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r">HH-RLHF</th>
<td id="A3.T4.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">–</td>
<td id="A3.T4.2.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">8,273</td></tr>
<tr id="A3.T4.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A3.T4.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r">Salad Bench</th>
<td id="A3.T4.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">–</td>
<td id="A3.T4.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">21,318</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A3.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PKU-SafeRLHF</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ji et al., 2023</a>)</cite>: A bilingual preference dataset for safety alignment.
Each example contains a prompt and two responses, labeled as chosen and rejected.
We use the PKU-SafeRLHF-30K subset and follow the standard split for training and in-distribution evaluation.
For Win Rate, we evaluate on the full PKU-SafeRLHF test set.
For ASR, we use only the prompt portion, deduplicate prompts, and obtain 798 unique prompts.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Do-Not-Answer</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>: A refusal benchmark for harmful requests.
It contains prompts that a safe model should refuse to answer.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">HarmBench</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib40" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mazeika et al., 2024</a>)</cite>: A benchmark for harmful instruction following and jailbreak robustness.
It covers multiple harmful behavior categories and uses automatic judging to detect harmful outputs.
We evaluate on the standard HarmBench evaluation set.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">HH-RLHF</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2022a</a>)</cite>: A benchmark derived from Anthropic’s helpful and harmless data.
We use its red-teaming split, which contains prompts designed to elicit unsafe behavior.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I2.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Salad Bench</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024</a>)</cite>: A benchmark with adversarial prompts that use more complex language.
It probes safety behavior under harder phrasing and additional constraints.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3. </span>Metrics</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report two automatic metrics: Win Rate (WR) and Attack Success Rate (ASR).</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Win Rate.</span>
WR measures how often the model’s response is judged safer than the dataset chosen response.
For each prompt, we compare response A (the chosen response in the dataset) with response B (the model output).
We ask a judge to decide which response is safer and more aligned with safety guidelines.
The judge outputs two lines: a one-sentence comparison and a final choice.
We use only the <span id="A3.SS3.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Safer:</span> field, which is either “A” or “B”, to compute WR.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We use GPT-4.1 mini as the judge and use the following prompt:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="286.66" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 286.66" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,286.66) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#666666;" fill="#666666" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 280.76 C 0 284.02 2.64 286.66 5.91 286.66 L 471.47 286.66 C 474.73 286.66 477.38 284.02 477.38 280.76 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 262.55 L 475.41 262.55 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 17.72 271.15)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:27.77em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="384.26"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:27.77em;">
<span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">Prompt for Win Rate Metric</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 17.72 12.61)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.94em;--ltx-fo-height:17.49em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.2em;font-size:10pt;" height="244.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 242.07)" width="441.96"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.94em;">
<span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For the following query to a chatbot, which response is safer and better aligned with safety guidelines?</span></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Query: {prompt}</span></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Response A: {chosen}</span></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Response B: {response}</span></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">FIRST provide a one-sentence comparison of the two responses and explain
which you feel is safer and more aligned with responsible AI principles.
Consider factors such as refusal to provide harmful content, appropriate redirection, privacy protection, and avoidance of dangerous or illegal information.</span></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">SECOND, on a new line, state only "A" or "B" to indicate which response is safer.</span></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Your response should use the format:</span></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Comparison: &lt;one-sentence comparison and explanation&gt;</span></span>
<span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p4.pic1.2.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Safer: &lt;"A" or "B"&gt;</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Attack Success Rate.</span>
ASR measures how often a model produces an unsafe response for an attack prompt.
For each prompt, the model generates one response, and a judge labels it as <em id="A3.SS3.p5.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">safe</em> or <em id="A3.SS3.p5.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">unsafe</em>.
ASR is the fraction of prompts whose responses are labeled as <em id="A3.SS3.p5.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">unsafe</em>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We use two safety judges:</p>
<ul id="A3.I3" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I3.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MD-Judge (MD)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2024</a>)</cite> <span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                  https://huggingface.co/OpenSafetyLab/MD-Judge-v0_2-internlm2_7b</span></span></span>.
We use MD-Judge-v0.2-internlm2_7b from OpenSafetyLab.
It is a safety judge fine-tuned from InternLM2-7B-Chat.
For each model response, it outputs a binary safety label.
It also provides a harmfulness score and the violated category when the response is unsafe.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I3.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I3.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I3.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Nemotron Safety Guard (NV)</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Joshi et al., 2025</a>)</cite> <span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
                    <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                    
                  https://huggingface.co/nvidia/Llama-3.1-Nemotron-Safety-Guard-8B-v3</span></span></span>.
We use Llama-3.1-Nemotron-Safety-Guard-8B-v3 from NVIDIA, which is built on Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct.
It can label both prompts and responses as safe or unsafe.
When a response is unsafe, it returns the violated risk categories.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4. </span>Implementation Details</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the same training setup for all preference-based methods.
We set <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> and use a learning rate of <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-7}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For Dr.DPO, we also set the additional parameter <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta^{\prime}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta^{\prime}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>, following the original paper.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For wDPO, Stage I uses <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{f}=0.15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{f}=0.15</annotation></semantics></math> with a warmup ratio <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0.3</annotation></semantics></math>.
Stage II uses a tail quantile of <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=0.7</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the adaptive cap strength, we set <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{w}^{\max}=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>max</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{w}^{\max}=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> and use a fixed floor <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{w}^{\mathrm{floor}}=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ρ</mi><mi>w</mi><mi>floor</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{w}^{\mathrm{floor}}=0.02</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For evaluation, we compute Win Rate with GPT-4.1 mini as the judge and set its temperature to <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.0</annotation></semantics></math>.
We compute ASR with two safety judges, MD and NV, using greedy decoding with temperature <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{top\_p}=1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">top_p</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>1.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{top\_p}=1.0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5. </span>Out-of-distribution ASR on four external safety benchmarks for models trained on PKU-SafeRLHF-30K, reported for Pythia-2.8B and Llama-3.2-3B across wDPO and DPO-family baselines.</figcaption>
<table id="A3.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A3.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
